From: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
Subject: DEBUG: Trace the boot from the SPL to U-Boot proper

Temporary, do not merge. U-Boot proper of the iot-gate-imx8plus runs through
init_sequence_f and then the board restarts, without any readable output of its
console. Find where it stops and why it restarts:

- the SPL prints the reset cause of the previous boot (SRC_SRSR) as soon as it
  has a console, and clears it, so each boot shows its own
- the SPL prints where it jumps to and the first words found at U-Boot and at
  the FDT
- U-Boot proper writes a marker to UART2 between the steps of
  init_sequence_f and, before it relocates, the values that crt0 uses for the
  new stack and gd
- everything that U-Boot proper asks its console to print is also written to
  UART2 directly, and so is a system reset

---

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
@@ -292,2 +292,12 @@
 
+	/* DEBUG ONLY, remove after the investigation: what is jumped to */
+	printf("DBG jump: entry 0x%lx load 0x%lx size 0x%lx fdt 0x%lx flags 0x%x\n",
+	       (ulong)spl_image->entry_point, (ulong)spl_image->load_addr,
+	       (ulong)spl_image->size, (ulong)spl_image->fdt_addr,
+	       spl_image->flags);
+	/* 0xedfe0dd0 read as a word is the magic of a valid FDT */
+	printf("DBG jump: words at U-Boot 0x%08x 0x%08x, at the FDT 0x%08x\n",
+	       *(u32 *)CONFIG_TEXT_BASE, *((u32 *)CONFIG_TEXT_BASE + 1),
+	       spl_image->fdt_addr ? *(u32 *)spl_image->fdt_addr : 0);
+
 	if (spl_image->flags & SPL_FIT_FOUND) {
